A||||4||Shawn Alexander||Speedometer problems||||5||
Z||000000||Shawn Alexander||04-18-2000||09:26 PM||||Just picked up an 1988 formula. The stock<BR>5 speed was replaced with 1988 beretta<BR>5 speed and everything works fine but the<BR>speedo. At about 35-40mph the needle is<BR>pegged. I also noticed that down on the <BR>tranny the wires are spliced onto the<BR>speedo drive. I'm guessing that the beretta<BR>speedo drive is not compatible with the<BR>fiero. Anyone have any ideas on how to<BR>correct this problem.||||reg||5
Z||000001||TOM||04-18-2000||09:44 PM||||It may not have been spliced right. Either way send 88 database nut your info so the car can be added to the listing||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phil||04-18-2000||10:25 PM||||I'm about 90% sure that the Beretta trans uses a different type of speedo sender something like 45000 pulses/mile rather than the 4000 pulses/mile that the normal trans uses(different voltage too). You can either 1. pull the tranny split the case and change the pickup<BR>2.heard of a company that makes pulse converters(help someone)<BR>3. change to a different speedo (VDO makes a programable electronic one or maybe Cliff's)<BR>4. find someone that knows what the he*l they're talking about<BR>I don't think this is what you wanted to hear  BUT....||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||04-19-2000||12:59 AM||||From Rodney Dickman's site. <A HREF="http://www.execpc.com/~rodney1/getraginfo.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.execpc.com/~rodney1/getraginfo.htm</A> <P><B>Most front wheel drive Getrags use a steel pick-up cog on the differential carrier for the speedometer. This will need to be replaced with the plastic gear used in the Fiero. Any 85-88 Manual speedometer sending unit will work. The GM part # is S8672319, List $4.40. To install this gear, you will need to "split the case". I have all the necessary instructions to accomplish this task. While this sounds difficult, it is actually "very doable" for the average do-it-yourselfer. The correct sealant to use between the case halves when reassembling is Locktite 518 gasket eliminator flange sealant.</B><P>Pretty much what Phil said.<P><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 04-19-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||rcn491||04-19-2000||04:19 PM||||The pulse converter is made by Dakota Digital. See "Speedo error" thread.<BR>||||reg||1
